# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-models.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/568-default-the-execute-implement-stage-to-haiku-at-xhigh-effort-and-verify-to-opus-at-medium-effort/requirements.md
Feature: Default the execute implement stage to Haiku at xhigh effort and verify to Opus at medium effort

  @SCN001
  Scenario: New defaults apply when the file is absent
    Given a project without steering/sdlc-models.json
    When sdlc-models.mjs ensure creates it, or execute resolves stage models with the plugin defaults
    Then implement is haiku/xhigh and verify is opus/medium
    And start is haiku/default, deliver is haiku/xhigh, and repair is opus/default

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Missing keys are completed with the new defaults
    Given a valid steering/sdlc-models.json that lacks the implement or verify entry
    When upgrade completes the file
    Then the added entries are implement haiku/xhigh and verify opus/medium
    And every existing value is unchanged

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Upgrade offers to move entries holding an earlier default
    Given a valid steering/sdlc-models.json whose implement is opus/medium or whose verify is opus/high
    When /sdlc-upgrade-project runs detection
    Then it emits the sdlc-models-defaults refresh finding naming those stages
    And on approval the refresh writes implement haiku/xhigh and verify opus/medium, keeping every other value and the key order

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The current defaults and project-chosen values are never offered
    Given a valid steering/sdlc-models.json holding the current defaults or values that are not earlier plugin defaults
    When /sdlc-upgrade-project runs detection or the refresh runs
    Then no sdlc-models-defaults finding is emitted for those entries
    And the refresh reports already-current without writing

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Repository configuration and documentation state the new defaults
    Given the nmg-sdlc repository
    When steering/sdlc-models.json, README.md, workflows/onboard-project/WORKFLOW.md, and workflows/upgrade-project/references/detection.md are read
    Then they state implement haiku/xhigh and verify opus/medium as the defaults
    And the earlier-default examples name implement opus/medium and verify opus/high
